    "bj_payoff": 1.5,
    "skip_round_pdf_reason": "CDZ- versus CDP1 changes post-split policy only. Unsplit stand/hit/double do not use that policy. Answering CDZ=n skips possibly-wrong compute_pdf so a shoe can finish in batch."
  },
  "adapter_notes": [
    "BJDealer.computeProbabilities and BJPlayer keep the dealer upcard in the shoe. Hakimi remaining counts already exclude the upcard and the player's cards, and still include the unknown hole.",
    "possibly-wrong action values are a fraction of the original wager, conditioned on the dealer not having blackjack. Hakimi net EV uses the same unit. For A/T, Hakimi peek_negative=true.",
    "The released strategy.exe dealer table prints five decimals. EV queries print nine decimals in percent.",
    "Split EV uses CDZ-/CDP1/CDP, not Hakimi sequential two-hand total net. Those cells are not_directly_comparable."
  ],
  "tolerances": {
    "ev_abs": 1e-8,
    "dealer_raw_abs": 6e-6,
    "dealer_peek_abs": 1.5e-5,
    "internal_abs": 1e-10,
    "dealer_print_decimals": 5
  },
